# Cursor Rules — EC Marketplace

## Project
C2C e-commerce marketplace (Shopee-style). TypeScript monorepo: Express API (`ecommerce-api/`) + Next.js 14 (`ecommerce-web/`). Vietnamese UI.

## Stack
- Backend: Express + Prisma + PostgreSQL + Redis + JWT + Zod
- Frontend: Next.js 14 App Router + TailwindCSS + Zustand + React Query
- Infra: Docker Compose + Nginx

## Rules

### General
- Write TypeScript, no JavaScript
- Vietnamese for all UI text (labels, messages, placeholders, errors)
- English for code identifiers and comments
- Use existing patterns — check `hooks/`, `store/`, `components/` before creating new

### Backend (`ecommerce-api/`)
- Module pattern: `src/modules/[name]/` → routes.ts, controller.ts, service.ts, validation.ts
- Use `asyncHandler()` wrapper on all controller methods
- Use `ApiError.badRequest/unauthorized/notFound()` for errors
- Validate with Zod: `z.object({ body: z.object({...}), query: ..., params: ... })`
- Response helpers: `ok(res, data)`, `created(res, data, message)`

### Frontend (`ecommerce-web/`)
- `"use client"` on all interactive components
- Data fetching → React Query hooks in `hooks/` (NOT useEffect + useState)
- Client state → Zustand stores in `store/` with persist middleware
- Use `api` from `lib/api.ts` for HTTP calls (JWT auto-attached)
- Auth cookies synced from Zustand store for Next.js middleware
- TailwindCSS only, no CSS modules
- Color: Orange for shop UI, Indigo for landing sections
- Responsive: grid-cols-2 → sm:grid-cols-3 → lg:grid-cols-4 → xl:grid-cols-5

### Naming
- Components: PascalCase (`ProductCard.tsx`)
- Hooks: camelCase with `use` prefix (`useProducts.ts`)
- Stores: camelCase with `.store` suffix (`auth.store.ts`)
- Types: camelCase with `.type` suffix (`product.type.ts`)
- Routes: kebab-case in URLs

### Key Files
- DB schema: `ecommerce-api/prisma/schema.prisma`
- API routes: `ecommerce-api/src/routes/index.ts`
- Auth flow: `ecommerce-web/store/auth.store.ts` → `hooks/useAuth.ts`
- API client: `ecommerce-web/lib/api.ts`
- Route guard: `ecommerce-web/middleware.ts`
